  "prefLabel": "Bfc 103.02 Duties of the Board",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bfc 103.02 Duties of the Board.\n\n(a) The responsibilities of the board include:\n\n(1) Adopting jointly with the state fire marshal, and with the approval of the commissioner, pursuant to RSA 153:5, I, amendments to the state fire code described in RSA 153:1, VI-a;\n\n(2) Adopting rules pursuant to RSA 541-A relative to procedures of the board’s operation;\n\n(3) Reviewing and assessing the application of the state fire code and recommending legislation to modify the requirements of the state fire code; and\n\n(4) Acting in a continuing advisory capacity to the state fire marshal on any matters pertaining to his/her duties pursuant to RSA 153.\n\nSource. #10553-A, eff 3-25-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bfc100.html"
